    "sentence_translations": [
      "Why is it “Up to the Bathroom”, but “Down to the Kitchen”?",
      "",
      "“I want to go to the bathroom”, \"She is elegant around the guests, while also knowledgable in the kitchen”",
      "These are phrases we can hear daily.",
      "So why is it “up” to the bathroom, but “down” to the kitchen?",
      "",
      "Actually, there is a reason for this.",
      "In ancient China, people usually built the toilet in the north side of the courtyard, and the kitchen in the south side.",
      "And when going south people often say “go down south”.",
      "When going north, people say “go up north”.",
      "When going to the bathroom you go to the north of the courtyard, and therefore say “go up to the bathroom”.",
      "When going to the kitchen you go to the south of the courtyard, and therefore say “go down to the kitchen”.",
      "",
      "Even though nowadays the toilet is not necessarily in the north side, and the kitchen not in the south, ..",
      ".. the expressions “up to the bathroom” and “down to the kitchen” live on.",
      ""
    ]
